{
  "requirement": "`Fingerprint` pairs a digest with the scheme used to compute it. Each `NodeContents`\nimplementation chooses the scheme. Freshness checks compare both fields as opaque values.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Fingerprint {\n    pub scheme: String,\n    pub value: String,\n}\n\nimpl Fingerprint {\n    pub fn new(scheme: String, value: String) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Fingerprint;\nimpl Debug for Fingerprint;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for Fingerprint;\nimpl PartialEq for Fingerprint;\nimpl Serialize for Fingerprint;\nimpl Eq for Fingerprint;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Obligations and the tests that cover them:\n\n1. **Freshness compares both fields as opaque values.**\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors]` stores a node dependency with fingerprint `fp(\"same\")`.\n   - The record is current when scheme and value both match.\n   - It is not current when the scheme differs but the value is the same: `Fingerprint::new(\"other\",\"same\")`.\n   - It is not current when the value differs but the scheme is the same: `fp(\"changed\")`.\n   - Each case asserts `is_current`'s boolean outcome, so a check that ignored either field would fail.\n   - I read `dependencies_are_current` in `src/graph.rs`. It uses one `!=` comparison for both node and outgoing-edge dependencies, so the node-dependency test covers the shared comparison.\n\n2. **Struct shape and trait implementations.**\n   - `Fingerprint` has public `scheme` and `value` fields, `new`, and `#[non_exhaustive]`.\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the public exports against the spec's inventory. It also compiles the Habeas consumer against the SDK.\n   - `Serialize` and `Deserialize` are covered by `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs#fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]`. That test stores a `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` holding `Fingerprint::new(\"targets-v1\",\"preserved\")` and asserts the loaded dependencies equal the stored ones.\n   - `PartialEq` is exercised by that equality assertion and by the freshness comparison.\n   - `Clone`, `Debug`, `Eq` and the `#[non_exhaustive]` attribute come from derive and attributes on `struct[Fingerprint]`. They contain no conditional or transformation, so they need no separate test.\n\n3. **Each `NodeContents` implementation chooses the scheme.** This belongs to the `NodeContents` requirements. `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint` is also cited by the wildcard test, and it is outside this requirement's scope.\n\nI found no unexercised obligation and no assertion that contradicts the text.",
